    "detailed_description": "<strong>Cat Got Your Tongue is an old-school horror point-and-click game.</strong> And let me tell you, you'll feel what it's like to be in the wrong place at the wrong time.<br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2930140/extras/019335c9e2ecc0d130a6f46558c75b4d.poster.avif?t=1734955644\" width=600 height=338 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2930140/extras/019335c9e2ecc0d130a6f46558c75b4d.webm?t=1734955644\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2930140/extras/019335c9e2ecc0d130a6f46558c75b4d.mp4?t=1734955644\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Turn your screen brightness to the fullest...</h2><br>My previous game was &quot;too bright,&quot; so I decided to make this one the darkest and the gloomiest.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >No complicated puzzles.</h2><br>There are no intricate puzzles in this game, but there's intricate gameplay where you, as the player, will have to figure things out. The game is built on exploring rooms and memorizing them. Look for items and use them to avoid a deadly fate.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Because, you're not alone in the house...</h2><br>There's something bigger and thicker living here, something more evil, and hungry... lurking in the shadows. The House Cat. Playing tag with it, you should run immediately if you don't want to end up in someone's trash.",
    "about_the_game": "<strong>Cat Got Your Tongue is an old-school horror point-and-click game.</strong> And let me tell you, you'll feel what it's like to be in the wrong place at the wrong time.<br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2930140/extras/019335c9e2ecc0d130a6f46558c75b4d.poster.avif?t=1734955644\" width=600 height=338 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2930140/extras/019335c9e2ecc0d130a6f46558c75b4d.webm?t=1734955644\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2930140/extras/019335c9e2ecc0d130a6f46558c75b4d.mp4?t=1734955644\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Turn your screen brightness to the fullest...</h2><br>My previous game was &quot;too bright,&quot; so I decided to make this one the darkest and the gloomiest.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >No complicated puzzles.</h2><br>There are no intricate puzzles in this game, but there's intricate gameplay where you, as the player, will have to figure things out. The game is built on exploring rooms and memorizing them. Look for items and use them to avoid a deadly fate.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Because, you're not alone in the house...</h2><br>There's something bigger and thicker living here, something more evil, and hungry... lurking in the shadows. The House Cat. Playing tag with it, you should run immediately if you don't want to end up in someone's trash.",
